From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Synkar <dev@synkar.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 20:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm: display: select SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC for HDMI audio helper

DRM_DISPLAY_HDMI_AUDIO_HELPER registers a platform device named
HDMI_CODEC_DRV_NAME ("hdmi-audio-codec") via drm_connector_hdmi_audio_init(),
which is bound by the hdmi-codec ASoC codec driver (CONFIG_SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC).

That symbol is hidden (no prompt) and is only selected by the legacy
DRM_DW_HDMI_I2S_AUDIO path, not by the QP bridge used on rk3588. As a result,
on rk3588 (DRM_DW_HDMI_QP + DRM_DISPLAY_HDMI_AUDIO_HELPER) the codec platform
device stays unbound and the hdmi0-sound simple-audio-card defers forever
("asoc-simple-card: parse error").

Select SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC from DRM_DISPLAY_HDMI_AUDIO_HELPER so the codec
driver is built whenever the helper is, matching the runtime dependency.

Signed-off-by: Synkar <dev@synkar.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/display/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/Kconfig
@@ -79,6 +79,7 @@ config DRM_DISPLAY_HDCP_HELPER
 config DRM_DISPLAY_HDMI_AUDIO_HELPER
 	bool
+	select SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC if SND_SOC
 	help
 	  DRM display helpers for HDMI Audio functionality (generic HDMI Codec
 	  implementation).
